  "design": {
    "channel": "one embedding row per CN, added to the atom input beside metal_bias",
    "dropout": "cn_conditioning_dropout replaces a row with the null token; drawn from a LOCAL generator seeded by (shuffle_seed, epoch)",
    "guidance": "v = v_uncond + s*(v_cond - v_uncond), s = cn_cfg_scale (YAML key, default 1.0)",
    "null_token": "row 0 is zero, and is both the bit-exactness device and the CFG unconditional branch",
    "realised_cn": "the metal's degree in the DECODED RDKit molecule, not a CN head: the graph is the output, so a head would answer a different question",
    "row_init": "1/sqrt(H) from a LOCAL generator, so constructing the module draws no global RNG"
  },
  "honest_limits": [
    "The smoke is 64 clouds x 7 epochs on CPU. It establishes wiring, not obedience: the decoded mean CN is 2.1 at every request because the checkpoint is 7 epochs old.",
    "conditional_success at one request is gameable. MEASURED: request 2 scores 0.750 while requests 4 and 6 score 0.062 and 0.031, and the decoded mean CN is ~2.13 in all three cells. The T8 gate therefore has to be the dose-response range, not a single cell.",
    "velocity_sensitivity is a property of the network on random positions, not of the sampler: it says the condition can reach the output, not that training used it.",
    "cn_request_override and cn_cfg_scale are eval-time keys; the training loop always conditions on the template's own CN, with dropout."
  ],
  "metric": "wfa112_cn_conditioning_smoke",
